1
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:34,482
<i>There are an estimated 8 million people
in the five boroughs of New York.</i>

2
00:02:34,691 --> 00:02:37,277
<i>12 million in the
greater metropolitan area.</i>

3
00:02:37,736 --> 00:02:40,446
<i>There are almost 10 million
telephone exchange lines.</i>

4
00:02:40,905 --> 00:02:43,157
<i>Over 50 phone services.</i>

5
00:02:43,408 --> 00:02:46,367
<i>3 million New Yorkers
are cell phone users.</i>

6
00:02:46,577 --> 00:02:49,790
<i>It used to be a mark of insanity
to see people talk to themselves.</i>

7
00:02:50,247 --> 00:02:55,627
<i>Now it's a mark of status. And speed dial
is quickly replacing the drop of a coin.</i>

8
00:02:55,836 --> 00:02:58,507
<i>Despite increased usage
of cellular devices...</i>

9
00:02:58,716 --> 00:03:02,301
<i>... an estimated 4.5 million residents
and 2 million visitors...</i>

10
00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:06,680
<i>... still utilize pay phones
on a regular basis.</i>

11
00:03:11,478 --> 00:03:14,272
<i>This is the telephone booth
at 53rd and 8th...</i>

12
00:03:14,479 --> 00:03:18,692
<i>... perhaps the last vestige of privacy
on Manhattan 's West Side.</i>

13
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:22,196
<i>It is the last booth of its type,
still in regular operation.</i>

14
00:03:22,404 --> 00:03:25,200
<i>Up to 300 calls daily originate here.</i>

15
00:03:25,408 --> 00:03:29,827
<i>This location has been burglarized
41 times in the last six months.</i>

16
00:03:30,037 --> 00:03:32,665
<i>Verizon has scheduled this structure
to be torn down...</i>

17
00:03:32,874 --> 00:03:36,585
<i>... and replaced with a kiosk
as of 8 a.m. Tomorrow.</i>

18
00:03:36,794 --> 00:03:38,670
<i>Hardly two blocks away...</i>

19
00:03:38,879 --> 00:03:42,925
<i>... meet the man who is to be
the final occupant of that booth.</i>

20
00:03:43,134 --> 00:03:45,470
Donny. Donny. Donny, listen to me.

21
00:03:45,677 --> 00:03:49,263
I said I'd get you magazine coverage,
and I'm getting you in a magazine.

22
00:03:49,473 --> 00:03:52,477
Look, you gotta trust me.
No means yes to these people.

23
00:03:52,685 --> 00:03:54,519
Get "What's Up?" magazine
on the line.

24
00:03:54,728 --> 00:03:55,812
Yeah, I heard you.

25
00:03:56,021 --> 00:03:58,106
Donny, I got "What's Up?" magazine
on the line.

26
00:03:58,315 --> 00:04:00,566
They wanna know about you,
so I'm hanging up.

27
00:04:00,984 --> 00:04:03,612
This is Erica or Lars.
I can't tell the difference.

28
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:05,531
- You got Stu.
- We said no.

29
00:04:05,739 --> 00:04:08,200
I didn't hear you,
so I'm giving you a second chance.

30
00:04:08,409 --> 00:04:10,034
- We don't do magicians.
- Magicians?

31
00:04:10,244 --> 00:04:13,662
Donny G is an artist who happens
to look like a supermodel.

32
00:04:13,872 --> 00:04:16,875
"- The New Guys" is offering him the cover.
"- New Guys" wants him?

33
00:04:17,084 --> 00:04:19,544
And I haven't told my client,
my favorite client...

34
00:04:19,753 --> 00:04:23,047
...that I am making this call, all right?
He wants "New Guys."

35
00:04:23,214 --> 00:04:25,300
I want you and I can make him
come around...

36
00:04:25,468 --> 00:04:28,596
...but you'll lose us if I don't
hear from you by end of business.

37
00:04:28,845 --> 00:04:31,348
Get "New Guys". Tell him "What's Up?"
Is offering a cover.

38
00:04:31,515 --> 00:04:32,974
Okay. Big Q.

39
00:04:33,225 --> 00:04:37,312
Adam, I know three people looking
for dog walkers. That could be you.

40
00:04:37,563 --> 00:04:40,858
"Sit. Stay. Don't worry, Fluffy,
I'll clean your shit and wipe your ass."

41
00:04:41,107 --> 00:04:43,152
- You got Stu.
- What's up with my party, Stu?

42
00:04:43,359 --> 00:04:46,153
I was just telling my assistant
to get my favorite client...

43
00:04:46,321 --> 00:04:48,574
...on the phone,
and here you are. Nice.

44
00:04:51,033 --> 00:04:54,286
Listen. Seriously, we gotta look
at a new night for your release party.

45
00:04:54,495 --> 00:04:57,709
There are two premieres, a fundraiser.
All the happening places are booked.

46
00:04:57,916 --> 00:04:58,958
If we move the date...

47
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:02,504
Voodoo on you-do, motherfucker,
from Big Q to Big Stu!

48
00:05:02,713 --> 00:05:04,923
- Big Q, be reasonable.
- Motherfucker, I'm a gangster!

49
00:05:05,130 --> 00:05:08,718
- I don't gotta be reasonable!
- You're cutting out.

50
00:05:08,927 --> 00:05:12,848
Next time I'm gonna kill your cracker-ass
if you keep talking about me like that!

51
00:05:13,056 --> 00:05:14,348
Right?

52
00:05:14,599 --> 00:05:17,894
N.Y.P.D. Blue, 11 o'clock.

53
00:05:18,268 --> 00:05:21,522
Stuey, the hardest working
PR guy. How's business?

54
00:05:21,732 --> 00:05:24,192
How many times I have
to tell you, Wyatt? I'm a publicist.

55
00:05:24,401 --> 00:05:25,943
- Tickets.
- Tickets.

56
00:05:26,151 --> 00:05:28,153
Four for Britney Spears, right?

57
00:05:28,362 --> 00:05:30,365
You put the "Ho"
in show business, Stuey.

58
00:05:30,573 --> 00:05:33,533
It's Stu. What do you got for me?

59
00:05:33,744 --> 00:05:38,706
They just checked Mrs. Sharp
into Bellevue again.

60
00:05:38,914 --> 00:05:41,418
- Page Six. Tell Britney I send my love.
- All right.

61
00:05:41,627 --> 00:05:43,293
Enjoy the show.

62
00:05:44,004 --> 00:05:47,340
Hold on a sec. Page Six, this is Lana.

63
00:05:47,547 --> 00:05:50,885
Bless you. Lana, it's Stu Shepard.
Bless you.

64
00:05:51,094 --> 00:05:52,887
- Is it you or your boss calling?
- It's me.

65
00:05:53,097 --> 00:05:55,180
I'm looking for some
mutual back-scratching.

66
00:05:55,388 --> 00:05:59,102
You get my privileged N.Y.P.D. Blue
info and I get you to save my ass.

67
00:05:59,309 --> 00:06:00,978
Not now, Stu. I'm a sick woman.

68
00:06:01,187 --> 00:06:03,065
This is going
to make you feel better.

69
00:06:03,272 --> 00:06:07,067
Tony-winning producer Jeffrey Sharp
tossed his wife back into drug rehab.

70
00:06:07,275 --> 00:06:09,443
Nice. What do you want
for that little tidbit?

71
00:06:09,652 --> 00:06:12,948
You better be nice to me while I'm on
the way up and taking your calls.

72
00:06:13,157 --> 00:06:16,493
The higher the monkey climbs,
the more you see of his ass.

73
00:06:16,702 --> 00:06:17,953
Have a heart, Lana.

74
00:06:18,162 --> 00:06:21,957
Listen, today my half-wit assistant
faxed you regarding my favorite client.

75
00:06:22,166 --> 00:06:24,293
Great singer,
about to turn great actress.

76
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:27,796
- Another little Miss Tits and Ass?
- Look, I'm on cell, no names.

77
00:06:28,005 --> 00:06:31,300
That was strictly in-office information.
You didn't print it, did you?

78
00:06:31,507 --> 00:06:34,135
- I got it.
- All right, tell me Richard didn't see it.

79
00:06:34,343 --> 00:06:36,180
He didn't put it in the column?

80
00:06:36,387 --> 00:06:38,598
Stu's on the phone,
scared he's gonna lose his job.

81
00:06:38,807 --> 00:06:41,142
His office sent you something
by mistake. He wants it.

82
00:06:41,351 --> 00:06:44,479
You tell him T.F.B.
Put that at the top of the column.

83
00:06:44,688 --> 00:06:46,481
- Stu, it ran, sorry.
- Yeah?

84
00:06:46,690 --> 00:06:48,942
- Oh, God. Oh, no.
- I'm really sorry.

85
00:06:49,151 --> 00:06:50,902
Yes!

86
00:06:51,778 --> 00:06:55,156
"What's Up?" magazine offered Donny G
a photo in "What's Hot and Happening."

87
00:06:55,365 --> 00:06:58,077
- Fuck them. Make them sweat.
- He's on a conference call.

88
00:06:58,243 --> 00:07:01,705
He could take a while. Yeah, can he call
you back? Okay. All right, bye.

89
00:07:01,913 --> 00:07:03,165
- Pretty smooth.
- Thank you.

90
00:07:03,373 --> 00:07:05,459
If you can absorb
everything I teach you...

91
00:07:05,624 --> 00:07:09,087
...focus and get a new wardrobe,
you can make it big in public relations.

92
00:07:09,254 --> 00:07:10,840
- I got a sense.
- Cool. Cool. Cool.

93
00:07:11,048 --> 00:07:12,215
- Up, T?
- How you doing, man?

94
00:07:12,424 --> 00:07:14,218
Mario's!

95
00:07:15,758 --> 00:07:17,844
Hey! Hey! Hey! Not so fast, Stu!

96
00:07:18,096 --> 00:07:21,391
How come you run every time
you go past my place, huh?

97
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,685
- Because I'm busy, Mario.
- Yeah?

98
00:07:23,894 --> 00:07:26,146
Well, no more drinks or free meals, okay?

99
00:07:26,355 --> 00:07:30,066
One lousy mention in the "Post",
you expect to eat for six months? No!

100
00:07:30,526 --> 00:07:33,612
Mario, maybe I could throw
the hippest party this month your way.

101
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:36,363
- Stu.
- No, I couldn't. My clients would kill me.

102
00:07:36,614 --> 00:07:40,243
- What hip party?
- It's just Big Q, the hottest new rap star.

103
00:07:40,451 --> 00:07:43,205
- There'll be local TV coverage...
- Nine and 11.

104
00:07:43,413 --> 00:07:45,624
MTV, BET, VH1.

105
00:07:45,831 --> 00:07:48,501
But I promised other clients,
people who actually pay me.

106
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:51,086
- No, you owe me.
- It's gotta be the night of the 18th.

107
00:07:51,295 --> 00:07:54,299
Toss in a buffet for 80 people,
record company will pick up the booze...

108
00:07:54,508 --> 00:07:56,175
...and I will deliver you celebrities.

109
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:59,260
Anything you want, okay?

110
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:02,682
Expand the menu, wallpaper
those bathrooms, for God's sake.

111
00:08:02,932 --> 00:08:04,726
You only get one shot
with celebrities.

112
00:08:05,226 --> 00:08:07,354
Thank you. Thank you, Stu!

113
00:08:07,562 --> 00:08:09,230
- That was fucking brilliant.
- Listen.

114
00:08:09,481 --> 00:08:12,649
Call Big Q. Tell him we got him
the hippest place in town on his date.

115
00:08:12,858 --> 00:08:14,027
- Call "What's Up?"
- Yeah.

116
00:08:14,235 --> 00:08:15,486
We'll take their offer.

117
00:08:15,695 --> 00:08:17,989
Messenger a bottle of Jameson's
to Lana at Page Six...

118
00:08:18,196 --> 00:08:20,490
...with a note saying... Write this down.
- Got it.

119
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:24,412
- Irish chicken soup. Love, Stu.
- "Irish chicken soup. Love, Stu."

120
00:08:24,621 --> 00:08:26,539
- All right, no harm being gracious.
- Yeah.

121
00:08:26,748 --> 00:08:29,083
Okay. Actually, better off,
deliver it over yourself.

122
00:08:29,291 --> 00:08:31,293
- Get to know the players.
- I'll do that.

123
00:08:31,502 --> 00:08:32,794
Thank you for teaching me.

124
00:08:33,003 --> 00:08:35,800
- And, Adam, don't you have a suit?
- Actually, no.

125
00:08:36,049 --> 00:08:37,926
Here. Get yourself one.

126
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:41,053
- I'm gonna start paying you soon.
- Yeah, I hope so.

127
00:08:41,261 --> 00:08:44,180
- You got a bunch of messages.
- I'm late for a meeting. Hold them.

128
00:08:44,431 --> 00:08:45,474
- All right.
- All right.

129
00:08:45,683 --> 00:08:49,144
- See you, Stu!
- See you, Adam!

130
00:09:18,423 --> 00:09:20,467
- Excuse me.
- I'm trying to make a call here.

131
00:09:20,675 --> 00:09:23,886
This is for you. Half-pepperoni,
half-mushroom, extra crisp.

132
00:09:24,095 --> 00:09:26,597
You ever heard of delivering
a pizza to a phone booth?

133
00:09:26,764 --> 00:09:28,141
I don't think so.

134
00:09:28,349 --> 00:09:32,313
Gentleman occupying phone booth,
53rd, between Broadway and 8th.

135
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:34,814
It's a mistake.

136
00:09:35,274 --> 00:09:38,066
What am I supposed to do
with the pie? It's all paid for.

137
00:09:38,317 --> 00:09:40,236
There's a homeless guy
around the block.

138
00:09:40,445 --> 00:09:44,158
Give him the pizza and say "You can turn
away, but you can't make it go away."

139
00:09:44,367 --> 00:09:47,327
He'll think I'm trying to poison him.
They always get that idea.

140
00:09:47,494 --> 00:09:49,954
Get off the fucking pizza, all right?

141
00:09:51,206 --> 00:09:53,458
That language is uncalled for.

142
00:09:53,667 --> 00:09:55,542
Holy shit!

143
00:09:55,751 --> 00:09:59,171
I'm sorry. Please return to sender.

144
00:09:59,381 --> 00:10:01,466
Fuck off.

145
00:10:02,384 --> 00:10:06,888
Here you go, $5. Eat the pizza yourself.
You look like you could use a good meal.

146
00:10:26,282 --> 00:10:27,282
Hello.

147
00:10:27,534 --> 00:10:31,828
Pam, could you believe some nut case
just tried to deliver me a pizza?

148
00:10:32,037 --> 00:10:36,042
Why are you always in the same
phone booth, same time, every day?

149
00:10:36,250 --> 00:10:40,254
- Well, it's quitting time, right?
- Thank God, we were mobbed today.

150
00:10:40,462 --> 00:10:41,630
So how's your day?

151
00:10:41,838 --> 00:10:44,716
It's getting better
by the minute, sweetheart.

152
00:10:44,925 --> 00:10:47,178
Who's the most famous person
you publicized today?

153
00:10:47,387 --> 00:10:49,472
- You.
- Really?

154
00:10:49,681 --> 00:10:53,057
I told a few columnists Mel Gibson
was looking for actresses for his film.

155
00:10:53,308 --> 00:10:57,063
And I said the possibilities
were Cameron Diaz, Julia Roberts...

156
00:10:57,272 --> 00:10:59,857
...and my favorite client, you.

157
00:11:00,065 --> 00:11:01,191
You didn't really do that.

158
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,610
First step toward being noticed
is being mentioned.

159
00:11:03,821 --> 00:11:05,945
I just got out of a
conference at the City Hotel.

160
00:11:06,111 --> 00:11:07,741
I was thinking you
could come down.

161
00:11:07,990 --> 00:11:11,869
There are a couple of people and a few
martinis I'd like to introduce you to.

162
00:11:12,077 --> 00:11:13,955
- Stu, I...
- Listen, Pam. Pam. Pam.

163
00:11:14,162 --> 00:11:16,456
It's about time we talked
about your career. Come on.

164
00:11:16,665 --> 00:11:22,087
I feel awful but I promised my scene
partner that I would rehearse for class.

165
00:11:22,295 --> 00:11:25,591
We're doing a scene from "Jerry Maguire."
I'm playing Renée Zellweger's part.

166
00:11:25,757 --> 00:11:28,469
That's great. Look, I rescheduled
a meeting to see you...

167
00:11:28,677 --> 00:11:30,555
...but I guess I can reschedule it back.

168
00:11:30,764 --> 00:11:33,140
- Are you mad?
- Don't worry about it. I'm not mad.

169
00:11:33,306 --> 00:11:34,891
Maybe tomorrow.

170
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:36,435
Yeah, later.

171
00:11:36,684 --> 00:11:38,186
- Look, Stu...
- What?

172
00:11:38,395 --> 00:11:39,980
Big kiss.

173
00:11:40,189 --> 00:11:41,648
You too.

174
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,744
<i>- Yeah.
- Isn't it funny?</i>

175
00:11:54,954 --> 00:11:57,413
<i>You hear a phone ring,
and it could be anybody...</i>

176
00:11:57,622 --> 00:12:00,208
<i>... but a ringing phone has to be
answered, doesn't it?</i>

177
00:12:00,416 --> 00:12:01,459
What?

178
00:12:01,667 --> 00:12:04,212
<i>I hope you realize
how you've hurt my feelings.</i>

179
00:12:04,419 --> 00:12:07,924
<i>- Who the fuck is this?
- Don't think about leaving that phone.</i>

180
00:12:08,132 --> 00:12:10,676
<i>- Wrong number, pal.
- It was a perfectly delicious pizza.</i>

181
00:12:10,885 --> 00:12:13,055
<i>You're certainly going
to wish you had accepted it.</i>

182
00:12:13,263 --> 00:12:16,557
Naturally, this is part of the gag.
The pizza bit. That was funny shit.

183
00:12:16,767 --> 00:12:19,937
<i>Well, its purpose was to keep
your strength up for what's coming next.</i>

184
00:12:20,186 --> 00:12:23,272
<i>- What's coming next is I'm hanging up.
- Oh, no, you won't.</i>

185
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:26,360
<i>- You're going to learn to obey me.
- Obey you?</i>

186
00:12:26,568 --> 00:12:29,111
<i>- Who is this?
- Someone who enjoys watching you.</i>

187
00:12:29,321 --> 00:12:30,363
Watching me?

188
00:12:30,570 --> 00:12:34,700
<i>Yes, I love the suit you're wearing today.
Black on raspberry sorbet. Very Italian.</i>

189
00:12:35,868 --> 00:12:37,786
Where...? Where are you?

190
00:12:37,995 --> 00:12:42,165
<i>There are hundreds of windows out there.
Why don't you check them out?</i>

191
00:12:46,796 --> 00:12:49,673
<i>- So, what am I doing now?
- You're scratching your head.</i>

192
00:12:49,881 --> 00:12:53,386
<i>Now you're brushing your hair back.</i>

193
00:12:54,470 --> 00:12:57,389
<i>That's not very nice, Stu.</i>

194
00:12:58,266 --> 00:12:59,642
Did you call me Stu?

195
00:13:00,684 --> 00:13:04,313
<i>- Who's Stu? I don't know any Stu.
- Why, do you prefer Stuart?</i>

196
00:13:04,522 --> 00:13:06,607
A lot of people in this
neighborhood know me.

197
00:13:06,773 --> 00:13:10,444
<i>Stuart Shepard, 1326 West
51st Street, Third Floor, front.</i>

198
00:13:10,653 --> 00:13:13,696
<i>- Go mind-fuck some other guy, pal.
- I know Pamela McFadden too.</i>

199
00:13:13,905 --> 00:13:16,783
<i>It's not in your best interest
to disconnect me.</i>

200
00:13:17,033 --> 00:13:19,328
<i>Someone could get hurt.</i>

201
00:13:19,537 --> 00:13:22,332
<i>What's the matter, Stu?</i>

202
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:25,251
If you're some fucked-up,
failed actor I wouldn't handle...

203
00:13:25,417 --> 00:13:28,962
...or some prick intern I fired, I will
hunt you down and I will crush you.

204
00:13:29,171 --> 00:13:31,006
You will never work in this town.

205
00:13:31,214 --> 00:13:32,634
I can turn people into gods...

206
00:13:32,841 --> 00:13:36,344
...and I can turn you into a total
fucking loser if you weren't one already.

207
00:13:36,595 --> 00:13:39,808
Do you hear me?
Am I upsetting you? Hello.

208
00:13:40,015 --> 00:13:43,017
Oh, you think I'm gonna, what?
Pay you off or something?

209
00:13:43,227 --> 00:13:45,979
<i>- Tell me what you want.
- Now you want to talk to me.</i>

210
00:13:46,187 --> 00:13:48,272
Did Adam at my office
put you up to this?

211
00:13:48,481 --> 00:13:51,151
<i>No, I thought this up all by myself.</i>

212
00:13:51,361 --> 00:13:52,862
Keep thinking. I'm hanging up.

213
00:13:53,069 --> 00:13:57,574
<i>I'll say hi to your wife, Kelly, for you.
Talk to you later.</i>

214
00:13:58,073 --> 00:14:00,158
What the...?

215
00:14:02,288 --> 00:14:05,498
<i>The callback feature
cannot be activated...</i>

216
00:14:05,916 --> 00:14:07,584
Motherfucker.

217
00:14:34,821 --> 00:14:39,531
<i>- Tell me what you want.
- I want your complete attention.</i>

218
00:14:40,783 --> 00:14:44,579
<i>- Are you an actor?
