1051
01:00:27,624 --> 01:00:29,710
- Want me to clear the streets?
- Yeah.

1052
01:00:29,918 --> 01:00:33,378
No, no, no. I don't want the sniper
to be aware of any of our movements.

1053
01:00:33,629 --> 01:00:35,213
He's already got position on us.

1054
01:00:35,465 --> 01:00:37,883
Let's not let him know
we know too much, okay?

1055
01:00:38,801 --> 01:00:40,636
- Hey, Jonah.
- Yeah.

1056
01:00:40,886 --> 01:00:42,387
Don't look up.

1057
01:00:45,390 --> 01:00:47,560
Get me sharpshooters
looking at those windows.

1058
01:00:47,810 --> 01:00:50,312
- You got it, captain.
- I'm gonna buy us some time here.

1059
01:00:50,563 --> 01:00:52,063
All right.

1060
01:00:58,613 --> 01:01:01,656
Stu! It's okay if I come out
and talk to you for a second?

1061
01:01:01,908 --> 01:01:03,659
<i>- I don't know.
- This guy is so lonely.</i>

1062
01:01:04,493 --> 01:01:08,288
<i>- All he wants to do is talk.
- You're walking through a bad dream...</i>

1063
01:01:08,496 --> 01:01:11,458
<i>... and you can't wake up.
- Now he's really testing my patience.</i>

1064
01:01:11,667 --> 01:01:13,669
You wanna wake up, Stu?

1065
01:01:13,877 --> 01:01:18,882
I wanna, but I got issues
I can't talk about.

1066
01:01:19,089 --> 01:01:24,012
- That your psychiatrist on the phone?
- Yeah, yeah. I'm paying him overtime.

1067
01:01:24,304 --> 01:01:27,264
That was pretty brave what you did.

1068
01:01:27,932 --> 01:01:30,727
I mean,
admitting all that stuff to your wife.

1069
01:01:30,936 --> 01:01:34,397
- It was liberating, right?
- Should've been.

1070
01:01:34,607 --> 01:01:37,650
Maybe if I could be more honest
with my wife then...

1071
01:01:37,817 --> 01:01:40,445
...I don't know,
something would've turned out different.

1072
01:01:40,695 --> 01:01:42,364
<i>Oh, please.</i>

1073
01:01:42,573 --> 01:01:46,283
- Trust is the key. You trust me, Stu?
"- Get this man a seat on" Oprah.

1074
01:01:46,492 --> 01:01:50,329
I wanna, but I got the issues
I can't talk about.

1075
01:01:50,579 --> 01:01:52,915
<i>Yes, lethal issues.
Tell him to stay back.</i>

1076
01:01:53,167 --> 01:01:55,169
Look, don't come any closer.

1077
01:01:55,418 --> 01:01:58,046
Hey, I don't wanna cause
or make anything harder for you.

1078
01:01:58,296 --> 01:02:01,924
<i>Pam, Ramey, Kelly, people on the
street, you've got lives in your hands.</i>

1079
01:02:02,300 --> 01:02:05,345
I told you it's a private conversation.
What the fuck do you want?

1080
01:02:05,637 --> 01:02:09,098
I wanna let you know that it's safe
outside the booth.

1081
01:02:09,349 --> 01:02:11,517
<i>- It's not.
- It's always, "Get out of the booth!"</i>

1082
01:02:11,725 --> 01:02:14,520
I like it in the fucking booth!
All right? It's my world.

1083
01:02:14,729 --> 01:02:17,148
This is my booth, and
I'm not coming out. All right?

1084
01:02:17,440 --> 01:02:19,192
- Never.
- We're not gonna force you out...

1085
01:02:19,734 --> 01:02:21,987
...because there could be
some miscalculation...

1086
01:02:22,152 --> 01:02:25,366
...and then I would never find out
why this happened.

1087
01:02:26,116 --> 01:02:31,829
Stu, I'm afraid. I'm afraid
that I'm gonna be standing by...

1088
01:02:32,037 --> 01:02:35,958
...and my men are gonna shoot
some guy...

1089
01:02:36,208 --> 01:02:42,508
...and when we find out what's in his
hand, once we turn over his body...

1090
01:02:42,757 --> 01:02:45,259
...and we see what he was
threatening people with...

1091
01:02:45,468 --> 01:02:48,846
We realize that it was just
a little black Bible.

1092
01:02:49,388 --> 01:02:53,184
<i>- Or a cell phone.
- Don't push me, Stu.</i>

1093
01:02:56,604 --> 01:02:58,272
I'm not gonna let that happen here.

1094
01:02:58,814 --> 01:03:00,899
I wanted to make a phone call.
One lousy call...

1095
01:03:01,150 --> 01:03:03,152
<i>That's enough, Stu.</i>

1096
01:03:03,403 --> 01:03:07,657
- You got some bad news on that call?
- The worst.

1097
01:03:07,947 --> 01:03:09,867
I bet you want to jump off the edge.

1098
01:03:11,118 --> 01:03:13,746
<i>- I've been falling ever since.
- I'm gonna push him over the edge.</i>

1099
01:03:13,995 --> 01:03:15,497
<i>Just say the word.</i>

1100
01:03:15,706 --> 01:03:17,124
It's time to land.

1101
01:03:17,624 --> 01:03:21,002
- When you hit bottom, you die.
- I'm your safety net.

1102
01:03:21,211 --> 01:03:24,173
<i>Oh, please, say the word.</i>

1103
01:03:24,423 --> 01:03:27,634
If I tell you what you wanna know,
you'll die too.

1104
01:03:27,883 --> 01:03:30,053
<i>Exactly.</i>

1105
01:03:33,014 --> 01:03:34,684
- I'm going.
- Good.

1106
01:03:36,727 --> 01:03:39,937
But, Stu, we put a call out
to your lawyer.

1107
01:03:40,188 --> 01:03:42,274
Your wife, she gave us the number.

1108
01:03:43,610 --> 01:03:50,198
And I got my best men working
on bringing him down. Okay?

1109
01:03:51,032 --> 01:03:52,952
<i>That's it. The captain gets a bullet.</i>

1110
01:03:53,493 --> 01:03:54,912
Get out of here!
Hear what I said, asshole?

1111
01:03:55,119 --> 01:03:59,206
<i>- Get out of here, go on, now! Go!
- Enough of this sideshow, Stu.</i>

1112
01:03:59,457 --> 01:04:03,461
<i>- Your sins have caught up to you.
- So this is all some religious thing?</i>

1113
01:04:03,628 --> 01:04:07,089
<i>That explains it. Bible-crazed killer
picks on fashion-obsessed PR guy.</i>

1114
01:04:07,340 --> 01:04:09,761
<i>- Tell me what you want, then.
- What everyone wants...</i>

1115
01:04:09,969 --> 01:04:12,219
<i>... for the bad guy
to get what he deserves.</i>

1116
01:04:12,428 --> 01:04:14,514
<i>Go for the gun.</i>

1117
01:04:14,765 --> 01:04:16,849
<i>- Kill myself?
- Yes.</i>

1118
01:04:17,058 --> 01:04:19,227
It would be a rare, unselfish act.

1119
01:04:23,939 --> 01:04:26,567
- We got hostile action.
- Nothing is hostile until I say it is.

1120
01:04:27,277 --> 01:04:29,612
<i>- Look, I can't find it.
- Kelly, Pam, bam! Bam!</i>

1121
01:04:29,821 --> 01:04:31,906
All right! Look, I found it. I got it.

1122
01:04:32,157 --> 01:04:35,201
<i>- Then let's see it. Let everyone see it.
- The cops'll kill me.</i>

1123
01:04:35,451 --> 01:04:38,914
<i>Yes.
You're talking prime-time material now.</i>

1124
01:04:39,164 --> 01:04:40,999
<i>- All this shit just to watch me die?
- No.</i>

1125
01:04:41,249 --> 01:04:46,420
<i>To get you to do what's right.
If you wanna save yourself, confess.</i>

1126
01:04:46,671 --> 01:04:49,132
<i>- I already told Kelly everything.
- Everything?</i>

1127
01:04:49,381 --> 01:04:52,342
<i>No. No more excuses
and half-truths, Stuart.</i>

1128
01:04:52,593 --> 01:04:56,388
<i>You look out into those cameras
and you bare your soul.</i>

1129
01:04:56,638 --> 01:04:59,268
<i>TV seems to help bring out
the worst in people.</i>

1130
01:04:59,517 --> 01:05:01,186
<i>You should be fine.</i>

1131
01:05:01,435 --> 01:05:04,814
- How're those techs doing? Anything?
- No, not yet. Not yet.

1132
01:05:05,106 --> 01:05:09,527
We haven't found your lawyer yet,
Stu. But we're getting close. Okay?

1133
01:05:09,735 --> 01:05:13,906
<i>Stuart, I'm offering you a chance
to redeem yourself.</i>

1134
01:05:14,240 --> 01:05:16,784
<i>Come on, humble yourself
in front of your loved ones...</i>

1135
01:05:17,034 --> 01:05:21,456
<i>... and millions of strangers and me.
It's do-or-die time.</i>

1136
01:05:21,704 --> 01:05:23,791
What, you couldn't find anyone
worse than me?

1137
01:05:24,041 --> 01:05:27,002
Not a murderer or a child molester
but a publicist...

1138
01:05:27,210 --> 01:05:29,545
...who has fantasies
about pretty little actresses.

1139
01:05:30,006 --> 01:05:32,426
Who spends money on Italian suits
and dry cleaning...

1140
01:05:32,674 --> 01:05:35,969
...so people think he's important.
Who doesn't waste time being nice...

1141
01:05:36,220 --> 01:05:38,555
...to people who are of no use to him.
These are my crimes?

1142
01:05:38,721 --> 01:05:43,810
<i>Stuart, I know your crimes. Tell them.</i>

1143
01:06:07,876 --> 01:06:10,295
I've never done anything for anybody...

1144
01:06:10,586 --> 01:06:13,089
...who couldn't do something for me.
I string along...

1145
01:06:13,381 --> 01:06:16,510
...a kid with promises
that I'll pay him money.

1146
01:06:16,760 --> 01:06:18,846
I keep him around because he
looks up to me.

1147
01:06:19,013 --> 01:06:23,267
Adam, if you're watching, don't be
a publicist. You're too good for it.

1148
01:06:23,434 --> 01:06:29,397
I lie in person and on the phone.
I lie to my friends.

1149
01:06:29,606 --> 01:06:33,776
I lie to newspapers and magazines who
sell my lies to more and more people.

1150
01:06:33,985 --> 01:06:39,282
I'm just a part of a big cycle of lies.
I should be fucking president.

1151
01:06:39,532 --> 01:06:44,036
I wear all this Italian shit because
underneath, I still feel like the Bronx.

1152
01:06:44,328 --> 01:06:46,873
I think I need these clothes,
and this watch.

1153
01:06:47,164 --> 01:06:51,837
My $2000 watch is a fake,
and so am I.

1154
01:06:52,210 --> 01:06:55,090
I neglected the things
I should've valued most.

1155
01:06:55,381 --> 01:06:57,132
I valued this shit.

1156
01:06:58,176 --> 01:07:04,474
I take off my wedding ring to call Pam.
Kelly, that's Pam.

1157
01:07:06,266 --> 01:07:08,520
- Somebody got a 20 on this Pam?
- Don't blame her.

1158
01:07:08,770 --> 01:07:11,022
I never told her if I was married,
and if I did...

1159
01:07:11,272 --> 01:07:12,941
...she would've told me to go home.

1160
01:07:14,859 --> 01:07:19,195
Kelly, looking at you now,
I'm ashamed of myself.

1161
01:07:21,074 --> 01:07:26,954
I mean, I work so hard on this image,
on Stu Shepard, the asshole...

1162
01:07:27,162 --> 01:07:32,085
...who refers to himself in third person,
that I only proved I should be alone.

1163
01:07:33,170 --> 01:07:36,965
I've been dressing up as something
I'm not for so long...

1164
01:07:37,215 --> 01:07:40,843
...I'm so afraid you won't like what's
underneath.

1165
01:07:41,052 --> 01:07:46,183
But here I am.
I'm just flesh and blood and weakness.

1166
01:07:48,684 --> 01:07:50,435
I love you so fucking much.

1167
01:07:56,733 --> 01:08:02,197
I take off this ring because it only
reminds me of how I've failed you.

1168
01:08:02,446 --> 01:08:05,327
And, I don't wanna give you up.

1169
01:08:05,535 --> 01:08:09,621
I wanna make things better,
but it may not be my choice anymore.

1170
01:08:10,455 --> 01:08:13,000
You deserve better.

1171
01:08:28,432 --> 01:08:31,810
<i>- You're not gonna let me go.
- No.</i>

1172
01:08:32,019 --> 01:08:35,814
You never were.
I know a thing about lies.

1173
01:08:36,023 --> 01:08:37,941
I know a thing or two
about liars as well.

1174
01:08:38,150 --> 01:08:40,859
<i>Then why the confession?</i>

1175
01:08:46,951 --> 01:08:49,369
I didn't do it for you.

1176
01:08:51,204 --> 01:08:53,206
- Right there.
- Yeah, got that.

1177
01:08:53,456 --> 01:08:57,377
Captain, captain. The call to his wife
originated at 2: 17...

1178
01:08:57,628 --> 01:08:59,962
...at a hard line from the old
Barkley Hotel.

1179
01:09:00,172 --> 01:09:02,341
- You got a room?
- 604.

1180
01:09:02,798 --> 01:09:05,342
Second window from the corner.
ESU units holding.

1181
01:09:05,969 --> 01:09:07,469
Bring them in from 52nd Street.

1182
01:09:07,721 --> 01:09:11,098
Cover the windows, doors, fire escape,
every goddamn point of exit.

1183
01:09:11,349 --> 01:09:14,144
- ESU, ESU, come in from the 52nd...
- Stu!

1184
01:09:14,435 --> 01:09:17,062
- Your lawyer's coming down now!
- Doors, fire escapes...

1185
01:09:17,313 --> 01:09:18,565
Now!

1186
01:09:19,316 --> 01:09:21,568
<i>At least you'll die
with a clean conscience.</i>

1187
01:09:21,777 --> 01:09:25,071
No, you're the one that's gonna die!
Listen, you can hear them now.

1188
01:09:25,321 --> 01:09:26,989
They're coming to get you. Know why?

1189
01:09:27,198 --> 01:09:29,533
<i>- Because I sent them!
- You can't stop lying, can you?</i>

1190
01:09:29,784 --> 01:09:31,869
I can't stop lying?
They're coming up the stairs.

1191
01:09:32,077 --> 01:09:33,747
They're coming to get you.
Look around.

1192
01:09:33,995 --> 01:09:35,832
That room's getting smaller
every second.

1193
01:09:36,082 --> 01:09:37,415
Inch by inch! You know what?

1194
01:09:37,625 --> 01:09:40,420
It's not gonna be any bigger
than this fucking goddamn booth!

1195
01:09:40,712 --> 01:09:43,214
- They're in position, in position.
- Get them to move!

1196
01:09:49,888 --> 01:09:51,723
<i>- There's nobody there.
- There's nobody there?</i>

1197
01:09:51,932 --> 01:09:54,725
They're coming through that fucking
door to put you out of your misery.

1198
01:09:54,976 --> 01:09:57,437
You got a couple seconds left.
What're you gonna do?

1199
01:09:57,687 --> 01:10:00,313
<i>If this is true, I have to take someone
with me, don't I?</i>

1200
01:10:00,563 --> 01:10:03,943
<i>Since Kelly is the most important thing
in your life, I'll take her.</i>

1201
01:10:04,192 --> 01:10:06,654
Then take me! Take me.
This is about me!

1202
01:10:07,446 --> 01:10:10,073
I'm the fucking one you want!
Take me!

1203
01:10:10,282 --> 01:10:12,785
This is about me! Come on!

1204
01:10:13,077 --> 01:10:14,996
Take me! It's me you want!

1205
01:10:51,572 --> 01:10:53,741
This is Captain Ramey.
Somebody talk to me.

1206
01:10:54,034 --> 01:10:56,036
<i>We're too late.
The psycho heard us coming...</i>

1207
01:10:56,286 --> 01:10:58,206
<i>... and slashed his throat
with a knife.</i>

1208
01:10:58,413 --> 01:11:01,792
<i>- What's his condition?
- Critical. He's lost a lot of blood.</i>

1209
01:11:02,000 --> 01:11:04,419
Get him down here.
I don't want nobody dying on me.

1210
01:11:04,626 --> 01:11:06,046
All right.

1211
01:11:07,215 --> 01:11:09,633
- Kelly, where's Kelly?
- Your wife's fine, all right?

1212
01:11:09,883 --> 01:11:11,718
All right, try not to sit up.

1213
01:11:13,761 --> 01:11:15,930
- What hit me?
- Rubber bullet.

1214
01:11:16,139 --> 01:11:19,184
Figured if somebody's gonna
shoot you, it might as well be us.

1215
01:11:19,435 --> 01:11:21,520
Thanks.

1216
01:11:21,853 --> 01:11:23,854
- Did you get him?
- You did.

1217
01:11:24,357 --> 01:11:26,817
- I didn't do anything.
- Give yourself some credit.

1218
01:11:27,066 --> 01:11:30,445
Got yourself out alive.
Doesn't always happen that way.

1219
01:11:33,739 --> 01:11:35,408
- Are you okay?
- It's okay. I'm okay.

1220
01:11:35,658 --> 01:11:37,827
God. I was so afraid.

1221
01:11:38,077 --> 01:11:40,413
I thought I wasn't ever
gonna see you again.

1222
01:11:40,622 --> 01:11:42,373
Me too.

1223
01:11:42,624 --> 01:11:44,126
We've got things to talk about.

1224
01:11:44,667 --> 01:11:46,835
I only want to talk about
what you want to tell me.

1225
01:11:47,086 --> 01:11:51,174
I want to tell you everything.
Everything.

1226
01:11:52,341 --> 01:11:54,595
Get that gurney over here.
Get over here.

1227
01:11:54,802 --> 01:11:56,720
We lost him.

1228
01:11:59,014 --> 01:12:00,517
- I want to stand up.
- I got him.

1229
01:12:00,766 --> 01:12:02,768
- Sure you can hold on?
- I gotta see him.

1230
01:12:02,976 --> 01:12:05,062
- You don't want to see this.
- Yes, I do.

1231
01:12:05,270 --> 01:12:06,855
- Take it easy.
- Yes, I do.

1232
01:12:07,106 --> 01:12:10,318
- Allow me. Allow me.
- Go ahead.

1233
01:12:16,073 --> 01:12:18,492
You recognize him?

1234
01:12:18,701 --> 01:12:21,662
Yeah. He was down here trying
to deliver me a pizza...

1235
01:12:21,911 --> 01:12:23,997
...10 minutes before I got the call.

1236
01:12:24,206 --> 01:12:26,625
I told him to fuck off.

1237
01:12:26,835 --> 01:12:28,418
That's enough these days.

1238
01:12:33,798 --> 01:12:35,968
Just give it a minute.

1239
01:12:36,176 --> 01:12:38,346
We'll be driving,
and you'll be flying.

1240
01:12:38,554 --> 01:12:40,807
Whatever you say.

1241
01:12:44,100 --> 01:12:46,813
What a piece of shit.

1242
01:13:15,798 --> 01:13:17,884
Nice shoes.

1243
01:13:22,388 --> 01:13:24,307
Italian.

1244
01:13:26,518 --> 01:13:29,312
You hung up, Stu.

1245
01:13:29,521 --> 01:13:32,148
I didn't get a chance to say goodbye.

1246
01:13:33,901 --> 01:13:36,693
I feel bad about the pizza guy.

1247
01:13:37,278 --> 01:13:40,574
But I couldn't miss seeing
you and Kelly reunited.

1248
01:13:40,825 --> 01:13:43,702
You don't have to thank me.
Nobody ever does.

1249
01:13:43,952 --> 01:13:47,580
I just hope
your newfound honesty lasts.

1250
01:13:47,789 --> 01:13:52,378
Because it if doesn't,
you'll be hearing from me.

1251
01:14:20,988 --> 01:14:22,990
<i>Isn't it funny?</i>

1252
01:14:23,241 --> 01:14:27,660
<i>You hear a phone ring,
and it could be anybody.</i>

1253
01:14:28,371 --> 01:14:32,791
<i>But a ringing phone
has to be answered, doesn't it?</i>

1254
01:14:34,877 --> 01:14:37,338
<i>Doesn't it?</i>

1255
01:15:01,320 --> 01:15:02,279
Hello?
